{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB15566 - MONDO_4773",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone Acetate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Iridocyclitis (disease) through a chain of indications that link it to Fluorometholone and subsequently to the disease. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone Acetate may be used in the treatment of Idiopathic Uveitis, a condition that is itself associated with Iridocyclitis. This relationship is supported by the presence of a direct indication from Prednisolone Acetate to Idiopathic Uveitis, which in turn is linked to Fluorometholone, which is known to induce Iridocyclitis. The indirect pathway through Loteprednol Etabonate, though not directly indicated for Iridocyclitis, further reinforces the role of corticosteroids in the development of the disease. The cumulative evidence suggests that Prednisolone Acetate may contribute to the pathophysiology of Iridocyclitis through its anti-inflammatory effects, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
